03:07.490 --> 03:11.960
<b>Bout 14
"The Inter High Begins"</b>

03:13.740 --> 03:15.210
Okay, last one!

03:17.560 --> 03:20.460
Gojo-kun has a regimen set 
by his karate instructor,

03:20.460 --> 03:22.420
and Mitsuhashi-kun's 
doing strength training.

03:23.080 --> 03:25.970
They're all training individually 
after their group session with us.

03:26.410 --> 03:30.470
I'm sure they value their 
time training with the pros,

03:30.470 --> 03:33.650
but it thankfully isn't
enough to satisfy them.

03:34.100 --> 03:36.500
<i>Whether they know it or not,</i>

03:36.500 --> 03:41.650
<i>their losses at the team finals have
influenced them in a good way.</i>

03:42.270 --> 03:45.660
<i>I wonder what the other two are up to.</i>

03:46.090 --> 03:49.690
Well, looks like they've reflected on 
their actions, so I'll be going now.

03:52.100 --> 03:56.620
Unbelievable. I didn't expect 
you to actually call the police.

03:56.620 --> 03:58.570
You Odachi jerk!

03:58.570 --> 04:03.130
We got scared 'cause we thought some
luchadors had come to wreck up the place!

04:03.130 --> 04:04.310
Furthermore!

04:04.310 --> 04:08.320
That's the mask El Ultimo uses in MMA bouts!

04:08.320 --> 04:09.600
Oh, you can tell?

04:09.930 --> 04:12.830
Oh, wow, Odachi's got a female manager?

04:12.830 --> 04:16.150
You're a real cutie pie. 
And that mask looks great on you!

04:16.150 --> 04:17.810
Let's swap digits, yeah?

04:17.810 --> 04:19.260
Cool it, Takumi.

04:19.260 --> 04:20.610
Or your smartphone'll get smashed.

04:20.820 --> 04:25.610
<i>He said we were here to scout, 
so why'd we walk in through the front door?</i>

04:25.610 --> 04:34.250
<b>Devoted Souls are Victorious</b>

04:25.610 --> 04:34.250
<b>Kanazawa Kita High School 
Sumo Club</b>

04:26.180 --> 04:28.110
<i>This is Kanazawa Kita High School.</i>

04:28.110 --> 04:32.420
<i>They've triumphed at nationals in the past
and came third in last year's Inter High.</i>

04:32.420 --> 04:34.250
<i>They're a renowned sumo powerhouse!</i>

04:34.850 --> 04:36.750
Say, Captain Aizawa.

04:37.680 --> 04:40.570
How about we spar with them a little?

04:41.120 --> 04:43.880
I wanna show this chick my moves, you dig?

04:44.340 --> 04:48.850
And after Onimaru beat Tenma, 
I feel like we owe them some payback.

04:50.350 --> 04:51.540
Absolutely not.

04:51.540 --> 04:55.230
Kita High's here in Nagoya 
to get stronger, remember?

04:55.570 --> 05:00.230
We can't beat Odachi High here
and help make them stronger instead.

05:00.680 --> 05:01.750
What?

05:03.210 --> 05:07.480
Please let Onimaru know that
 I'm glad he beat Tenma.

05:07.900 --> 05:10.830
Losing is a great motivator 
for becoming stronger.

05:10.830 --> 05:13.660
So now, Tenma will get stronger.

05:14.470 --> 05:17.340
I won't tell anyone about the intrusion.

05:17.340 --> 05:20.920
I'd prefer to beat you in the ring 
than get your school suspended.

05:21.230 --> 05:22.680
So he says.

05:22.680 --> 05:24.050
What do we do, Captain?

05:24.050 --> 05:25.530
Huh? Who, me?

05:25.790 --> 05:27.250
Um...

05:27.250 --> 05:29.930
Could we fight just one bout?

05:29.930 --> 05:32.310
Like, some light, playful sparring?

05:34.020 --> 05:34.480
<b>Kanazawa Kita 
High School 
Sumo Club</b>

05:34.480 --> 05:39.060
<b>Kanazawa Kita 
High School 
Sumo Club</b>

05:34.830 --> 05:39.150
We're training our hearts out so that
our team comes out on top at nationals.

05:39.060 --> 05:39.730
<b>Kanazawa Kita 
High School 
Sumo Club</b>

05:39.150 --> 05:42.310
We have no time for "playful" sumo.

05:39.730 --> 05:43.480
<b>Kanazawa Kita 
High School 
Sumo Club</b>

05:43.840 --> 05:47.700
There's no comparison between our 
rich history, created by past sumo teams,

05:48.380 --> 05:53.450
and your nothing team who made it 
this far on dumb, beginner's luck alone.

06:02.140 --> 06:04.450
<i>I didn't expect us to walk out in silence.</i>

06:04.450 --> 06:07.650
<i>Kunisaki-san usually bites back.</i>

06:07.650 --> 06:09.540
So we're a nothing team?

06:12.610 --> 06:15.770
Yeah, I really can't take that lying down.

06:18.040 --> 06:20.400
Sorry. You two head on back without me.

06:23.350 --> 06:25.320
Looks like it worked.

06:26.510 --> 06:28.820
That guy was dead right.

06:28.820 --> 06:32.620
Kita High is prestigious, while we're
 basically nobodies with almost zero history.

06:32.920 --> 06:34.080
But...

06:35.220 --> 06:39.360
The captain isn't going to let anyone 
insult the history, however short it is,

06:39.360 --> 06:41.520
of the sumo club he founded!

06:41.520 --> 06:43.590
Isn't that right, Captain?

06:45.770 --> 06:49.080
<i>I know how prestigious Kita High is.</i>

06:49.080 --> 06:53.130
<i>But to call us a nothing team...</i>

06:53.130 --> 06:57.140
<i>They don't know what it's 
like to start from nothing!</i>

06:57.140 --> 06:58.480
<i>They know nothing!</i>

06:59.680 --> 07:03.550
<i>Two lonely years, then 
finally finding teammates...</i>

07:03.550 --> 07:06.480
<i>Through working together, 
we beat Ishi High.</i>

07:06.480 --> 07:09.670
<i>And he dares to say we're a nothing team?!</i>

07:09.670 --> 07:11.240
<i>We won't be handwaved away like that!</i>

07:14.330 --> 07:16.160
What is it? Forgotten something?

07:16.720 --> 07:20.040
Yeah, I forgot to say something important.

07:20.270 --> 07:24.010
Kanazawa Kita High won't be victorious
at nationals this year, either.

07:25.630 --> 07:28.180
Dachi High's sumo club is the strongest!

07:28.180 --> 07:31.010
And you'll find that out for yourselves
when we win at nationals!

07:35.380 --> 07:37.460
U-Uh, I mean...

07:38.150 --> 07:40.020
Don't look down on Dachi High!

07:40.020 --> 07:41.440
Th-That's all!

07:41.440 --> 07:43.020
E-Excuse me!

07:44.970 --> 07:48.190
Guess I went and said
something unnecessary again.

07:48.570 --> 07:51.980
The captain's the most determined guy here.

07:51.980 --> 07:56.240
I know how badly he wants
to declare that we're gonna win.

07:56.240 --> 08:00.830
Don't worry about that.
We all feel the same way.

08:01.040 --> 08:04.520
Yeah. We're going to emerge as champions.

08:05.200 --> 08:08.010
<i>We're not looking down on you, 
Odachi High School.</i>

08:08.420 --> 08:14.650
<i>We've studied Onimaru and the momentum
that took you past Ishi High.</i>

08:15.150 --> 08:16.760
<i>Very carefully, at that!</i>

08:18.890 --> 08:20.910
<i>Steel yourself for it already!</i>

08:20.910 --> 08:23.070
<i>I've told myself that so many times!</i>

08:23.070 --> 08:26.370
<i>I'm going to make Dachi High 
national champions!</i>

08:30.820 --> 08:32.570
Yes! Now, keep pushing!

08:36.350 --> 08:38.490
Okay, good.

08:38.490 --> 08:40.640
Don't forget that flow.

08:40.640 --> 08:42.230
Thank you very much!

08:42.710 --> 08:45.730
Jeez, do you even know how lucky you are?

08:45.730 --> 08:49.780
Getting to actually spar with 
Master Shibakiyama is a big deal.

08:50.320 --> 08:52.340
To be honest, I'm a little envious.

08:52.930 --> 08:55.920
Well, I need to get my exercise, too.

08:55.920 --> 08:59.760
I can still hold my own against
high-school students at least.

09:00.300 --> 09:02.870
Master, you really are incredible!

09:02.870 --> 09:06.190
Your instructions are more precise and 
easier to understand than our instructor's.

09:07.520 --> 09:10.230
His explanations are crude,
 and he's often inflexible.

09:10.230 --> 09:12.190
He's still got a lot to learn, hasn't he?

09:12.690 --> 09:13.730
Hey...

09:14.230 --> 09:16.380
Don't go comparing me to the master.

09:17.640 --> 09:19.440
It comes with age.

09:19.440 --> 09:22.040
You're still a first-year, aren't you?
You're on the right track!

09:22.440 --> 09:26.500
Man, I know I've got a lot to learn still.

09:27.300 --> 09:29.500
I'm trying my best here, dammit.

09:31.310 --> 09:33.110
Don't beat yourself up.

09:33.110 --> 09:36.050
Sure, there are things you can improve,

09:36.210 --> 09:39.930
but you're the one who put Dachi High 
in touch with the Shibakiyama Stable.

09:41.660 --> 09:47.310
And you can see for yourself how 
much better I've gotten since joining!

09:47.600 --> 09:50.690
True. You're working hard.

09:51.190 --> 09:52.540
It's not just me.

09:52.540 --> 09:54.330
We're all grateful to you, Instructor.

09:56.250 --> 09:57.590
Thank you very much.

09:58.720 --> 10:01.030
I'm expressing gratitude 
on behalf of the team.

10:01.500 --> 10:04.680
H-Hey, wh-what are you saying?

10:04.680 --> 10:08.260
Idiot. Save that gesture for 
when we stand victorious.

10:08.260 --> 10:10.630
We've got plenty more fights 
ahead of us. Sheesh.

10:12.420 --> 10:14.040
Excuse me, Master.

10:15.660 --> 10:18.340
Can we keep training for a little longer?

10:18.970 --> 10:21.770
I'd like you to spar with him, too.

10:23.070 --> 10:25.320
Wh-What do you mean?

10:29.090 --> 10:30.100
Hey, now...

10:30.100 --> 10:31.080
Don't go there.

10:31.080 --> 10:33.710
Is this because I said I was envious?

10:33.710 --> 10:35.530
You know about my condition.

10:35.690 --> 10:38.220
I can't fight for more than 20 seconds.

10:38.220 --> 10:39.490
I'm a defective sumo wrestler.

10:40.420 --> 10:42.160
Of course I know all that.

10:42.160 --> 10:44.830
But that's 20 whole seconds
you can use to fight.

10:46.690 --> 10:48.820
It's been bugging me for a while...

10:48.820 --> 10:53.700
Why didn't you put yourself down 
as a reserve for the Inter High?

10:51.960 --> 10:54.800
4

10:51.960 --> 10:54.800
<b>Ushio Hinomaru</b>

10:51.960 --> 10:54.800
5

10:51.960 --> 10:54.800
<b>Mitsuhashi</b>

10:51.960 --> 10:54.800
<b>Reserve</b>

10:55.010 --> 10:59.420
Even in our dojo, you haven't done any
sumo since you fought Hinomaru-san.

10:59.910 --> 11:00.930
Why is that?

11:02.280 --> 11:05.450
That's what I'm willing to 
sacrifice to be an instructor.

11:05.780 --> 11:08.760
Not listing myself as a team member
 shows how determined I am.

11:09.290 --> 11:12.310
I swore I'd focus on being an 
instructor so you guys can win.

11:13.100 --> 11:16.480
But you must still miss fighting.

11:18.430 --> 11:21.860
That intense look in your eye when you 
watched the captain and Hinomaru-san fight...

11:22.450 --> 11:24.200
That clenched fist...

11:24.720 --> 11:28.130
Was that really just how
you felt as an instructor?

11:28.870 --> 11:31.480
What is this? What's this about?

11:31.480 --> 11:33.790
Why are you trying to drag me into the ring?

11:34.260 --> 11:39.210
You aren't chickening out and 
asking me to take your place, are you?

11:39.810 --> 11:41.770
You know how I feel!

11:42.230 --> 11:44.580
I don't deny that I miss the sumo ring.

11:44.580 --> 11:48.110
But that's got nothing 
to do with the team!

11:49.600 --> 11:51.210
Nothing to do with us?

11:51.210 --> 11:52.750
How can you say that?

11:54.000 --> 11:56.640
Before we're instructor and pupils,

11:56.640 --> 11:59.230
we're all high-schoolers who love sumo!

11:59.710 --> 12:02.040
I want to respect your decision 
to be an instructor.

12:02.430 --> 12:04.740
But it's just not right!

12:05.580 --> 12:08.330
Why do you have to sacrifice so much for us?

12:09.060 --> 12:10.920
Don't carry it all on your shoulders!

12:10.920 --> 12:17.420
We're not so unreliable that we need 
you to suppress yourself for us, Kirihito!

12:18.970 --> 12:21.640
I'm not saying this out of pity.

12:21.980 --> 12:23.930
Hinomaru-san got injured, right?

12:24.300 --> 12:26.640
The same could happen to any one of us.

12:27.760 --> 12:33.480
It'd be a weight off all our minds if we had
a sixth team member we could rely on.

12:34.260 --> 12:37.120
Of course, I don't want to give up 
my place on the team sheet.

12:37.120 --> 12:39.180
I'll compete with you for it and make it mine.

12:39.660 --> 12:44.240
So let's all practice sumo together!

12:45.100 --> 12:45.690
I...

12:46.970 --> 12:47.830
I...

12:48.870 --> 12:50.740
Okay, get out here, Tsuji-kun.

12:52.320 --> 12:54.410
Oh, no, I didn't mean...

12:54.410 --> 12:56.220
I-I don't have a mawashi belt on...

12:56.220 --> 12:57.750
Never mind. Come as you are.

12:58.210 --> 13:02.760
I don't let just anyone spar with me.

13:06.400 --> 13:08.630
<i>Dammit all...</i>

13:11.050 --> 13:13.530
<i>There's no way I could
 refuse an offer like that!</i>

13:19.450 --> 13:20.400
Spirit!

13:23.310 --> 13:26.110
<i>How can a nearly 50-year-old man
headbutt so hard?!</i>

13:27.280 --> 13:30.530
<i>Damn, I'm so nervous, 
my breathing is erratic.</i>

13:30.530 --> 13:32.450
<i>I won't even last 20 seconds like this!</i>

13:34.410 --> 13:35.740
<i>You know I'm like this...</i>

13:36.610 --> 13:40.640
<i>And you guys are still saying I can fight?</i>

13:42.870 --> 13:43.740
<i>Guys...</i>

13:45.560 --> 13:46.860
<i>Thanks!</i>

13:55.310 --> 13:55.770
<b>Tokugetsu
Oxygen</b>

13:55.610 --> 13:56.500
Here!

13:55.770 --> 13:56.180
<b>Tokugetsu
Oxygen</b>

14:03.350 --> 14:05.790
M-Master... are you okay?

14:06.880 --> 14:10.200
I'll need to get Saenoyama to take you on.

14:10.410 --> 14:12.130
You're still a first-year.

14:12.130 --> 14:15.250
If you aren't sure what you want,
 try something different.

14:15.720 --> 14:18.960
But have you really not 
been doing any training?

14:18.960 --> 14:21.000
You're in really good shape.

14:21.310 --> 14:24.880
No, I did just enough to 
maintain my muscle mass.

14:24.880 --> 14:26.260
I see.

14:26.260 --> 14:28.970
I now understand why 
they're all so determined.

14:29.340 --> 14:31.970
Yes, he's strong!

14:32.480 --> 14:33.610
Stop that.

14:34.540 --> 14:36.390
<i>Our best formation...</i>

14:36.960 --> 14:39.220
<i>I don't know how much use I'll be to the team,</i>

14:39.620 --> 14:44.070
<i>but even as trainer, I'll do everything I can
 to help us to victory at nationals!</i>

14:46.940 --> 14:49.950
<b>Presenting</b>

14:46.940 --> 14:49.950
<b>Presenting</b>

14:46.940 --> 14:49.950
<b>S
a
e
n
o
y
a
m
a
-
z
e
k
i</b>

14:46.940 --> 14:49.950
<b>S
h
i
b
a
k
i
y
a
m
a
Stable</b>

14:47.390 --> 14:49.950
That week sure went fast.

14:50.230 --> 14:52.690
Are you really going back already?

14:52.690 --> 14:54.950
You could hang around and watch 
the Nagoya tournament.

14:56.040 --> 14:58.470
In order to put your lessons to good use,

14:58.470 --> 15:00.830
we need to continue our training.

15:01.800 --> 15:06.710
We pros will fight our battles,
 and you will fight your own.

15:07.000 --> 15:07.940
Yes, sir!

15:12.410 --> 15:14.510
I'm heading straight over to the karate dojo.

15:14.960 --> 15:17.090
We'll go to the school to train.

15:17.530 --> 15:19.560
I want to see what Hinomaru's learned.

15:20.250 --> 15:21.840
Before that, Kirihito...

15:22.510 --> 15:25.900
I want to see the video 
of Tottori Hakuro again.

15:26.190 --> 15:31.260
I want to sear the image of Tennoji-san, 
the opponent I must defeat, into my brain.

15:31.820 --> 15:34.460
I won't look away. I'll face him head-on.

15:37.130 --> 15:38.120
You got it.

15:38.710 --> 15:41.440
Come to think of it, where are
the captain and Kunisaki-san?

15:41.440 --> 15:43.630
They both got off the train already.

15:44.050 --> 15:46.250
They probably had stuff 
they wanted to work on.

15:46.630 --> 15:47.650
Which is fine.

15:48.080 --> 15:50.740
Each of us must figure out
what we're lacking,

15:51.110 --> 15:54.260
and do our very best to grow stronger.

15:54.620 --> 15:56.760
What is he doing? Sumo?

15:57.620 --> 15:58.720
What's wrong with him?

15:58.720 --> 16:00.560
Did he lose a bet or something?

16:00.790 --> 16:03.370
Mom, what's that guy doing?

16:03.370 --> 16:04.480
Don't look at him!

16:05.510 --> 16:07.730
<i>I'm gonna die of embarrassment.</i>

16:07.730 --> 16:11.510
<i>But if I can stay calm
while doing this, then...</i>

16:11.510 --> 16:13.860
<i>If confidence is what I lack,
 I just need to find some.</i>

16:13.860 --> 16:15.910
<i>I'm going to change myself!</i>

16:15.910 --> 16:17.910
<b>Sakamoto
Bone-setting
Clinic</b>

16:16.200 --> 16:17.910
Hello, Captain?

16:18.230 --> 16:21.480
Yeah, it's feeling much better.

16:21.480 --> 16:23.800
There was nothing wrong with the bone.

16:23.800 --> 16:26.380
I wish I'd taken part in 
the individual contest now.

16:28.090 --> 16:30.690
I'm joking! Don't fly off the handle.

16:30.690 --> 16:33.840
I'll be back in training tomorrow.

16:33.840 --> 16:34.590
Later!

16:35.010 --> 16:37.690
How about starting now instead of tomorrow?

16:37.690 --> 16:39.100
Mikazuki Munechika.

16:40.330 --> 16:42.600
This is the very best thing I can think of.

16:43.410 --> 16:46.110
Please. Help me train.

16:48.610 --> 16:50.360
<b>Ishigami
High
School
Sumo
Club</b>

16:49.090 --> 16:50.360
Jeez.

16:50.610 --> 16:53.360
I'm not captain anymore.

16:53.520 --> 16:55.850
Okay, back to training.

16:55.850 --> 16:56.660
Yes, sir!

16:57.310 --> 16:58.910
Yo, Captain Mamiya!

16:59.220 --> 17:01.240
Oh, Sanada-san!

17:01.240 --> 17:02.700
What are you doing here?

17:02.700 --> 17:03.580
Turn on the TV.

17:04.000 --> 17:05.600
There's something interesting on.

17:07.100 --> 17:10.880
If you want to sear Tennoji into 
your brain, this should help.

17:11.790 --> 17:15.500
<i>The hype surrounding high school 
sumo is reaching fever pitch.</i>

17:15.840 --> 17:19.300
<i>Today, we're visiting the 
powerhouse that is favorite</i>

17:16.180 --> 17:18.680
<b>Tottori Hakuro
Sumo Club</b>

17:18.680 --> 17:18.800
<b>Tottori Hakuro
Sumo Club</b>

17:18.800 --> 17:22.850
<b>Tottori Hakuro
Sumo Club</b>

17:19.300 --> 17:22.850
<i>to win a record seventh straight 
Inter High championship next month.</i>

17:22.850 --> 17:24.980
<i>This is Tottori Hakuro High School.</i>

17:25.360 --> 17:28.730
<i>The Tottori Hakuro sumo club 
is renowned as a place where...</i>

17:28.730 --> 17:33.350
<i>Mongolian exchange students train 
side-by-side with Japanese wrestlers.</i>

17:33.350 --> 17:35.340
<i>They've produced many 
pro sumo wrestlers,</i>

17:35.340 --> 17:37.110
<i>but of course, the best known is...</i>

17:37.460 --> 17:40.690
<i>the current strongest yokozuna, Jino-zeki.</i>

17:41.020 --> 17:46.440
<i>He visited his old school and trained
with the current team members.</i>

17:48.420 --> 17:50.540
He only spent a few seconds with shorty.

17:51.120 --> 17:55.380
Yokozuna Jino-zeki's 
attention was focused squarely

17:55.380 --> 17:58.050
on the strongest high
 school sumo wrestler:

17:58.480 --> 18:02.880
National treasure Dojikiri Yasutsuna,
AKA Tennoji Shido-kun.

18:02.880 --> 18:05.560
Hello, I'm the team's captain, Tennoji.

18:05.560 --> 18:07.100
<i>My, you </i>are<i> big, aren't you?</i>

18:07.100 --> 18:08.560
<i>Are you really a high school student?</i>

18:08.750 --> 18:12.820
Oh, no, there will be plenty 
of people my size at nationals.

18:13.340 --> 18:15.690
<i>I'm the favorite to win 
my third individual title,</i>

18:15.690 --> 18:17.410
<i>but it won't be easy.</i>

18:17.410 --> 18:19.250
<i>Everyone there will be a rival.</i>

18:19.890 --> 18:22.760
Talk about giving boring answers...

18:22.760 --> 18:23.830
<i>You're so modest.</i>

18:24.620 --> 18:28.160
<i>But you've won every official match 
you've contested since entering high school.</i>

18:28.160 --> 18:30.960
<i>Tell us, what's your secret?</i>

18:31.370 --> 18:33.180
My secret?

18:33.560 --> 18:36.720
I don't do anything special.

18:36.910 --> 18:39.340
<i>I'm not the son of a yokozuna,</i>

18:39.530 --> 18:41.470
<i>or the younger brother of an ozeki.</i>

18:41.770 --> 18:46.980
<i>If I had to pin down why, maybe it's because 
I love sumo more than anyone else.</i>

18:47.160 --> 18:52.410
I love sumo the most,
and I train the hardest.

18:53.190 --> 18:55.990
That's why I'm the strongest.

19:02.720 --> 19:06.000
<i>He's openly challenging the other
 high school sumo wrestlers.</i>

19:06.240 --> 19:08.450
<i>His humility is authentic,</i>

19:08.450 --> 19:11.750
<i>but under that dignified facade</i>

19:11.940 --> 19:12.820
<i>is a demon.</i>

19:13.210 --> 19:14.340
<i>I see.</i>

19:14.340 --> 19:16.580
<i>He's shackled by being a high-school athlete,</i>

19:16.580 --> 19:19.630
<i>but he has the unmistakable 
attitude of a yokozuna.</i>

19:20.200 --> 19:21.640
Just our luck.

19:21.940 --> 19:24.690
Why did we have to compete in this era?

19:24.690 --> 19:26.750
No, you've got it all wrong.

19:27.920 --> 19:30.780
It's Tennoji's continued position
at the top of the pile

19:30.780 --> 19:34.150
that has made those chasing him so strong.

19:34.540 --> 19:37.870
Without him, I wouldn't be where I am.

19:37.870 --> 19:39.610
So I'm grateful to him.

19:39.610 --> 19:44.210
Now, I'll take his head and become 
the strongest high school sumo wrestler!

19:47.510 --> 19:49.070
Just you wait, nationals.

19:49.700 --> 19:51.890
I'm coming for you with all I've got.

20:47.640 --> 20:48.850
<i>Are you watching me?</i>

20:49.260 --> 20:51.520
<i>I've come so far with this body.</i>

20:51.520 --> 20:57.270
<b>Ushio
Family
Grave</b>

20:52.200 --> 20:55.070
<i>I'll win the Inter High.</i>

21:01.610 --> 21:02.720
Go! Go!

21:02.280 --> 21:04.610
<b>National
High
School
Sports
Tournament</b>

21:02.280 --> 21:04.610
<b>National
High
School
Sumo
Championship</b>

21:02.720 --> 21:04.360
Do it!

21:06.570 --> 21:08.220
Yes, good work!

21:08.220 --> 21:09.370
That's one win!

21:11.810 --> 21:13.400
It's good to be back.

21:13.400 --> 21:15.830
I haven't been here since becoming 
the elementary school yokozuna.

21:16.020 --> 21:17.840
We're finally here.

21:18.020 --> 21:20.590
We get to do sumo here.

21:20.740 --> 21:23.760
Awesome. I'm all fired up!

21:24.940 --> 21:26.610
Don't let yourself get intimidated.

21:26.940 --> 21:30.040
All you have to do is
fight like we practiced.

21:30.040 --> 21:31.280
You're right.

21:32.990 --> 21:38.440
Okay! Let's show them how 
strong Dachi High's sumo club is!

21:38.780 --> 21:39.970
Yeah!

23:16.970 --> 23:18.360
<i>Everyone's looking at me.</i>

23:18.360 --> 23:20.790
<i>But I'm doing this to 
build up my confidence!</i>

23:20.790 --> 23:21.950
Hey, you there.

23:22.250 --> 23:23.920
What do you think you're doing?

23:24.560 --> 23:26.140
Oh, just some sumo training.

23:26.140 --> 23:27.260
Nothing suspicious!

23:27.420 --> 23:30.930
<b>Next Bout  "Onimaru Kunitsuna and Dojikiri Yasutsuna"</b>

23:27.600 --> 23:30.930
<i>This will </i>definitely<i> make
 me more confident.</i>
